    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "O ur editors and writers have lived across the globe, from Abu Dhabi to Toronto to São Paulo. So when we asked them to share beloved gifts from outside the US, the answers were as varied as our home towns."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This is the stuff we bring home in our suitcases and press into friends’ hands. Take the “workhorse” German paring knives or the bright red tortilla press that makes homemade masa feel effortless. There’s a 3lb tub of Maldon salt that is absurdly whimsical yet practical, and a set of Australian linen sheets that get softer with every wash."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Some picks, such as El Dorado rum from Guyana, are a little piece of home. Others, including posters from Denmark’s Louisiana Museum, are just beautiful. And all of them are delightful discoveries that don’t require a plane ticket to bring home."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Germany"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "‘Perfect workhorse’ knives from Solingen"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/95150df432dc6b6f2419d26cceda2065ba4a996e/0_0_2500_2500/1000.jpg?width=328&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/8c85e86186170d8810f7241b2e54f5580becf581/0_0_1185_1170/master/1185.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "Set of six knives with yellow, green and black gradient handles",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For more than 30 years, my parents have used these trusty German knives in the kitchen of our 10th-floor apartment in Abu Dhabi. Every household I know in the UAE has a set. You can pick up the whole collection at a local grocery store for next to nothing (they come in different colored handles!), and they’ll last a lifetime. They are incredibly versatile too – from slicing fruits and vegetables to cutting luggage tags and fixing things around the house. They don’t rust or lose their shape. Whenever I fly back from Abu Dhabi, I bring sets as gifts for my US friends. As a good friend in New York once put it: “They’re the perfect workhorse knife.” Maya Yang",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "these trusty German knives",
          "url": "https://go.skimresources.com/?id=114047X1771840&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.amazon.com%2FSMI-pcs-Professional-Vegetable-Solingen%2Fdp%2FB07VG1XGVQ%2Fref%3Dsr_1_7&sref=https://www.theguardian.com/thefilter-us/2026/nov/11/best-international-gifts&xcust=abTestParticipations%7Cfronts-and-curation-editorial-test%3Ab"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/95150df432dc6b6f2419d26cceda2065ba4a996e/0_0_2500_2500/1000.jpg?width=328&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Mexico"
