    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/f6501ed863d3c4f34ba276990247200cc2a21289/0_468_1400_1399/master/1400.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "Green bedding in bedroom",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "When I moved to Los Angeles, one of the first things that I bought was a linen sheet set from Dazed but Amazed, a small Australian company. The small-batch color combinations they offer are striking and unexpected; the sheets themselves get softer and softer with use. There’s a Pacific sensibility in everything the brand offers – they make my bedroom feel like it opens right on to the beach. Lois Beckett",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "linen sheet set",
          "url": "https://dazedbutamazed.com/collections/full-bed-set"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/c9e15807fdd36099c130256fdaa584888433c86f/0_0_2500_2500/1000.jpg?width=328&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
