    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/1feb018ab8173e83d61315640566cfadc7f5e2ce/0_0_1685_1685/master/1685.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "A 3lb tub of Maldon salt",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For your friends with caviar taste on a McNuggets budget, let me introduce you to the 3lb container of the UK’s Maldon sea salt flakes. While small boxes of Maldon salt are widely available at grocery stores around the US, loyalists to the stuff (me) know that the 3lb tub is a whimsical necessity in any good kitchen. It’s not only a visually fun gift to receive (it comes with a cute little handle!), it’s absurdly practical! I use a smaller salt cellar on my counter, but knowing there’s plenty to refill it with at all times? A thrill! It’s also roughly $30, making it a cost-effective gift for someone desperately seeking seasoning in their life, a white elephant offering or a cheeky pre-holidays gift from you to you. Jenna Amatulli",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "the 3lb container",
          "url": "https://go.skimresources.com/?id=114047X1771840&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.amazon.com%2FMaldon-Pyramid-Perfect-Hand-Harvested-Generations%2Fdp%2FB004SBQYMU%2Fref%3Dsr_1_2&sref=https://www.theguardian.com/thefilter-us/2026/nov/11/best-international-gifts&xcust=abTestParticipations%7Cfronts-and-curation-editorial-test%3Ab"
        }
      ]
    },
