      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/dd60f80d9a2654cb08ca88291148c3295a27b42c/0_0_1500_1354/master/1500.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "Pão de Queijo",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "I lived in Brazil in my 20s and 30s and to this day crave cheesy, gooey pão de queijo . This addictive treat , originally from the state of Minas Gerais, is a mix of tapioca flour, cheese and eggs. If I’m feeling particularly nostalgic I’ll pair them with some açai. I was delighted to find that this dry mix comes in bulk and tastes just like anything you’d find at a Brazilian padaria. DR",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "This addictive treat",
          "url": "https://go.skimresources.com/?id=114047X1771840&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.amazon.com%2Fdp%2FB008L1A0N2&sref=https://www.theguardian.com/thefilter-us/2026/nov/11/best-international-gifts&xcust=abTestParticipations%7Cfronts-and-curation-editorial-test%3Ab"
        }
