    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/e9087794a7461068d77d0e59406eaa08e18fc237/0_708_1450_1449/master/1450.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "Red moka pot next to mug of coffee topped with whipped cream",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "“Despite my Italian heritage, it took a temporary move to Rome to discover the magic of the moka pot. I instantly fell in love with this Italian coffee maker’s ability to brew a beverage on par with the $10 lattes found at my favorite cafes,” I wrote in my guide to achieving a perfect cup of iced coffee . In the chillier months, I rely on mine for achieving steaming cups of coffee, topped with frothed milk and a dash of cinnamon. It’s far less expensive than an espresso machine, but makes coffee nearly as strong. While I own two sizes, the colored option would make for a particularly great gift (I have red). Lauren Gould",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "achieving a perfect cup of iced coffee",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/thefilter-us/2026/apr/06/moka-pot-iced-coffee"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/5acf4397641dddc1014c2041030ba4aa5cf7473d/0_0_2500_2500/1000.jpg?width=328&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
