    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/2d7129eed71e7e9ac8b20c68a055e1d5e5c25b04/0_0_1500_1839/master/1500.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "Mango puzzles",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In the nearly 15 years I’ve lived in Toronto, I’ve never been more than 15 minutes by bike or streetcar from the city’s best outdoor spots: Trinity Bellwoods , or a ravine. These beautifully illustrated jigsaw puzzles that capture my favo(u)rite city scenes are a dream to play, each piece snapping easily into the next, and the poster is so lovely I have framed it. Jessie Willms",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Trinity Bellwoods",
