      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/bfbc22e709aaab9f6ee74cead1eccd079b4ab316/0_0_952_952/master/952.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none",
      "alt": "A Canadian e reader",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you’re looking for a non-Amazon alternative to the Kindle, let this be your sign to get a Kobo . (These e-readers are widely available outside Canada, but it’s nice to tell people that Canadian tech extends beyond the BlackBerry – RIP.) Then load it up with your favorite Canadian books, from Margaret Atwood to Rachel Reid to all the Emily St John Mandels. Does it also snow terribly from early December to May where you live? Get cozy under this quilt , in these sweatpants and this bunny hug (an endearing Saskatchewan regionalism for hoodie. Light a Province of Canada candle and read until spring. JW",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Kobo",
          "url": "https://go.skimresources.com/?id=114047X1771840&url=https%3A%2F%2Fereader.kobo.com%2Fen-us%2Fproducts%2Fkobo-clara-colour&sref=https://www.theguardian.com/thefilter-us/2026/nov/11/best-international-gifts&xcust=abTestParticipations%7Cfronts-and-curation-editorial-test%3Ab"
