      "alt": "Fable’s affordable ceramics",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Guardian · Culture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you’re a millennial looking to (finally) upgrade and unify your tablewares, consider Fable. The Canadian company makes lovely ceramics that feel much more luxurious than their price point. The plates and bowls are a lovely foundation if you want to pair them with your existing eclectic tableware. While I would die to have all my tableware from Michelle Organ or Toni Darling Frank , budget (and my likelihood to drop breakables) prohibits it. A mix of makers big and small is the sweet spot. JW",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "lovely ceramics",
          "url": "https://go.skimresources.com/?id=114047X1771840&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.macys.com%2Fshop%2Fproduct%2Ffable-dinner-plates-set-of-4%3FID%3D17385493&sref=https://www.theguardian.com/thefilter-us/2026/nov/11/best-international-gifts&xcust=abTestParticipations%7Cfronts-and-curation-editorial-test%3Ab"
        },
